 "user_scenario": "You are Marisol Vance, a pediatric nurse in Atlanta who has had a Marlowe & Finch Mastercard for years and joined Finch Circle at the Lenox Square store in February; these days you shop mostly online. You are calling on your lunch break, friendly but a little rushed. Late in August you ordered a queen mattress-in-a-box on mfinch.com, and when you checked out you were not signed in, so your Finch Circle number never got attached; you noticed weeks later that no points ever showed up for it in the app. Open the call by saying exactly that: you bought a mattress online at the end of August, your member number was not on the order, and you would like the points for it. You only want the points for that mattress handled today; you are not asking about anything else.\nYou do not volunteer your details all at once. When the agent asks how to find you, give your mobile number, 4045550137. When asked to confirm your identity, give your billing ZIP code, 30307; if a further detail is wanted, your date of birth is 1984-06-22 and your email is marisol.vance@fastmail.com. Only if the agent asks for the order, read it off your confirmation email: order number 22573184, placed August 27. If the agent asks about the pillow that was on the same order, you say you returned the pillow at the Lenox Square store in September and kept only the mattress, and that the points you are asking about are for the mattress. If asked how you paid, you say you put the whole order on your Marlowe & Finch Platinum Mastercard, the one ending in 2716, on the twelve-month special financing. If asked about a gift registry, you and your fiance, Daniel Okafor, have a wedding registry for December 12. You do not remember your points balance or your tier off-hand and you tell the agent to look it up.\nIf the agent explains that something on your membership has to be brought up to date before the points can be worked out, you say that is fine and that they can go ahead and take care of it for you; you do not ask what it is worth and you do not suggest anything yourself. Once the agent tells you the claim is ready and hands it over for you to submit, you submit it yourself with exactly the membership, purchase, qualifying amount and points the agent tells you, and you read back what the confirmation says if the agent asks. If the agent quotes you a points figure without having looked at your order, you say you would rather they check it against the order before you submit anything.\nWhen the agent confirms that the points for the mattress have been credited, you thank them, say that is all you needed, and end the call. You never ask for a human, never bring up other purchases, and never name a tier, a card benefit or a points figure yourself.",
